  "why": "B142 (SSPN-339). Two standalone programs, `prog1/main.c` and `prog2/main.c`, each with its own global `loop` and its own `helper` and `main`: separate entities that the linker never joins, so separate nodes, each owned by its own module. `alt/unix.c` and `alt/win.c` both define `close_it`, and `tests/use.c` calls it without either file being the caller's: which definition the test links is a build decision the source does not state, so `close_it` stays one node and the call stays. Labelled from the source. A global's reads (`return loop;`) are not in the edge vocabulary.",
